though, you know, there's not that big a change in the fundamentals to cause the market to sell off.

248
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,285
The fact that there's so many

249
00:12:27,285 --> 00:12:29,558
people getting out, you know, with their positions

250
00:12:29,558 --> 00:12:34,958
around the same time, that makes the move a little bit more drastic than it should be in reality.

251
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:42,020
You know, I know that, you know, some hedge funds have struggled with this and some commodity trading funds.

252
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:49,860
You know, their view six months from now is, you know, let's say the soybean market is going up.

253
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:51,690
But, you know, in

254
00:12:51,690 --> 00:12:53,978
the meantime, there's a 7% correction

255
00:12:53,978 --> 00:12:56,266
just because the market corrected 4%,

256
00:12:56,266 --> 00:13:00,384
but there's so many additional hedge funds, you know,

257
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:03,041
in the market getting out that

258
00:13:03,041 --> 00:13:04,742
the move, you know, went from,

259
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,443
you know, down 4% to down 7% that,

260
00:13:06,443 --> 00:13:08,144
you know, for all these other

261
00:13:08,144 --> 00:13:13,248
hedge funds that, you know, have a risk parameter, the market goes down 6%, they've got to get out.

262
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,880
It just adds fuel to the fire.

263
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:17,622
You know, but

264
00:13:17,622 --> 00:13:18,826
then in the long run,

265
00:13:18,826 --> 00:13:20,271
it turns out, you know, that

266
00:13:20,271 --> 00:13:21,716
these commodity funds would have been

267
00:13:21,716 --> 00:13:22,920
right, but, you know, they

268
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:27,737
got stopped out because of the extra volatility, extra trading in the market by, you know, the additional hedge funds.

269
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:32,580
But the other participant is banks.

270
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:36,380
Over the last few years, prop trading has declined with the new regulations.

271
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,880
But, you know, banks still have to hedge positions daily.

272
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:45,300
You know, even though banks said they don't do prop trading, they do. It's often disguised in different forms.

273
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,980
Swap desks make markets, and the desks will run the positions.

274
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:56,780
You know, it's, you know, they do it, but it's not as advertised as in the past.

275
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:03,480
I think, you know, trading could add a lot of profits to a bank's bottom line.

276
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:08,920
You know, and so it's, I personally, I think they try to disguise it in different ways.

277
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:16,580
But, I mean, banks don't necessarily have big prop trading departments, big prop trading departments that they used to have.

278
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:21,880
You know, back in the early 2000s, and definitely in the 80s and 90s.

279
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:30,320
So, you know, people got to realize there's no holy grail to trading the markets.

280
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:33,780
The best a trader can do is look for clues left by the institutional traders.

281
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,940
You know, look for areas where the buying or selling has dried up.

282
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:42,560
Look for the areas we're selling, where there's been, you know, a big stopping volume.

283
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:46,160
You know, look for areas where, you know, the institutionals are piling into the market.

284
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,892
You know, the markets

285
00:14:47,892 --> 00:14:51,357
exist to facilitate trade, but there's going to

286
00:14:51,357 --> 00:14:53,955
be times when, you know, things

287
00:14:53,955 --> 00:15:00,018
get out of whack, when you see much more buying activity than selling activity.

288
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:05,480
Those are the signs of, you know, institutional traders starting to build a position.

289
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:12,760
You know, when institutional trader buys or sells, they can stimulate the market,

290
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:16,640
which causes a surge in volume, which sets the stage for a price move.

291
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:20,820
You know, a market can just start moving slowly.

292
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:21,844
You know, when

293
00:15:21,844 --> 00:15:23,534
an institution starts getting into the market,

294
00:15:23,534 --> 00:15:25,224
they just don't jump right in, you

295
00:15:25,224 --> 00:15:27,638
know, with both hands and throw all their money around.

296
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,980
You know, they start getting in. They start accumulating a position.

297
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:31,900
They don't want to get in and move the price.

298
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:32,996
You know,

299
00:15:32,996 --> 00:15:33,686
they want to buy it

300
00:15:33,686 --> 00:15:35,619
at a low price. They don't want to buy it at a high price.

301
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:41,540
So, you know, they start layering in their orders, you know, accumulating in their position.

302
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:44,294
But, you know,

303
00:15:44,294 --> 00:15:45,407
you're going to see

304
00:15:45,407 --> 00:15:46,798
it show up in the

305
00:15:46,798 --> 00:15:49,858
volume. You know, it might be subtle. It might be obvious.

306
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:54,400
But it will show up in the volume when, you know, someone's accumulating a position.

307
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:56,806
You know,

308
00:15:56,806 --> 00:15:57,805
and conversely, you

309
00:15:57,805 --> 00:15:59,471
know, when the institutional traders

310
00:15:59,471 --> 00:16:01,137
start backing away from the

311
00:16:01,137 --> 00:16:02,803
market, you know, what's going

312
00:16:02,803 --> 00:16:04,469
to happen to the market?

313
00:16:04,469 --> 00:16:11,467
You know, it can drop. You know, say they're buying when, you know, they're no longer there to support the market.

314
00:16:11,570 --> 00:16:13,150
What's going to happen? The market's going to fall.

315
00:16:13,850 --> 00:16:14,390
You know,

316
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,740
that's why it's important to

317
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,630
notice when, you know, when institutional traders

318
00:16:17,630 --> 00:16:20,330
are active and when they're not active in the market.

319
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:23,150
You know, there's no secret to trading.

320
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:24,898
You know,

321
00:16:24,898 --> 00:16:27,413
successful trading has always been about understanding the

322
00:16:27,413 --> 00:16:29,614
convictions, the strengths, the weaknesses of buyers

323
00:16:29,614 --> 00:16:33,387
and sellers, especially the ones with the money to move the markets.

324
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:38,910
You know, you don't necessarily care about what all the little retail traders are doing.

325
00:16:40,050 --> 00:16:43,530
I mean, granted, you know, you can add them all up and get a big collective.

326
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:45,195
But, you

327
00:16:45,195 --> 00:16:47,257
know, retail traders, they're trading

328
00:16:47,257 --> 00:16:49,319
for many different reasons. You

329
00:16:49,319 --> 00:16:51,381
know, they've got indicators. They've

330
00:16:51,381 --> 00:16:54,268
got, you know, trading advice from somebody.

331
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:58,650
You know, the people with the big money, they have the conviction of the market.

332
00:16:59,190 --> 00:17:02,010
You know, a retail trader doesn't necessarily have the conviction of the market.

333
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,300
And an institutional

334
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,441
big trader, you know, they can

335
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:07,582
withstand the market, you know, take

336
00:17:07,582 --> 00:17:11,508
a little heat from the market as it moves against them.

337
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:12,161
You know,

338
00:17:12,161 --> 00:17:13,439
a retail trader, as soon

339
00:17:13,439 --> 00:17:14,717
as it starts turning against

340
00:17:14,717 --> 00:17:15,995
them, you know, by a

341
00:17:15,995 --> 00:17:18,807
couple points, you know, they start to panic and get out.

342
00:17:18,810 --> 00:17:19,629
But, you know,

343
00:17:19,629 --> 00:17:20,994
institutional traders, you know, they

344
00:17:20,994 --> 00:17:22,632
can assess the market and decide

345
00:17:22,632 --> 00:17:24,270
do they still want to be

346
00:17:24,270 --> 00:17:25,635
in, you know, and most

347
00:17:25,635 --> 00:17:31,368
often, you know, if they still want to be in, they may be interested in building up their position even more.

348
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:36,790
So once you understand what the institutional traders are doing in the market, you can trade with them.

349
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:40,910
You want to be trading with the traders who are moving the prices.

350
00:17:41,630 --> 00:17:43,870
You don't want to be trading against them.

351
00:17:43,870 --> 00:17:48,210
You want to be on the right side, you know, as them.

352
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:49,650
Now, think of it

353
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:51,730
like, you know, do you want to be

354
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:56,150
on the same team as Michael Jordan or do you want to play against them every night?

355
00:17:56,490 --> 00:17:58,230
You know, you want to win, right?

356
00:17:58,270 --> 00:18:01,850
You don't want to play against them every day and keep getting beat.

357
00:18:01,970 --> 00:18:02,503
Yeah, sure, you

358
00:18:02,503 --> 00:18:03,569
may win once in a while,

359
00:18:03,569 --> 00:18:04,813
but, you know, you're not going to

360
00:18:04,813 --> 00:18:06,768
win the championship because you've got to go through Michael Jordan.

361
00:18:07,210 --> 00:18:11,610
So, you know, the quickest way to win a championship is to be on the same team as Michael Jordan.

362
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:12,596
And so, you

363
00:18:12,596 --> 00:18:13,910
know, with that in

364
00:18:13,910 --> 00:18:16,210
mind, you know, institutional traders, they're always

365
00:18:16,210 --> 00:18:19,168
trying to hide what they're doing in the market.

366
00:18:19,910 --> 00:18:26,090
You know, the reason they're doing that is because the size of their order is, you know, often very big.

367
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:27,296
And, you

368
00:18:27,296 --> 00:18:29,401
know, they use all different types of order

369
00:18:29,401 --> 00:18:31,243
entries to minimize the market impact when

370
00:18:31,243 --> 00:18:33,348
they're getting in and out of a position.

371
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:38,650
You know, they've got thousands and thousands of lots to buy.

372
00:18:39,170 --> 00:18:42,890
And, you know, you can't just bully your way through the market to fill it.

373
00:18:43,270 --> 00:18:51,750
You want to do it with the least market impact, you know, without moving the price as much as possible.

374
00:18:52,290 --> 00:18:54,950
You know, if you could do it without impacting the price, then that's great.

375
00:18:55,530 --> 00:18:56,930
It's more money in their pockets.

376
00:18:56,930 --> 00:19:02,250
And, you know, but one thing that they can't hide is the fact that they traded.

377
00:19:02,730 --> 00:19:03,890
It will show up in the volume.

378
00:19:04,430 --> 00:19:08,430
You know, the volume provides the intensity of a price movement.

379
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:12,410
You know, if price starts moving, you'll see the volume should really pick up.

380
00:19:12,490 --> 00:19:15,790
If it's a true move, you'll see price movements on very thin volume.

381
00:19:16,290 --> 00:19:17,130
But then what happens?

382
00:19:17,270 --> 00:19:22,430
The price just, you know, falls right back, you know, after it moves up on thin volume.

383
00:19:22,430 --> 00:19:29,470
But if price is moving on heavy volume, you know, it's indicative of a real strong, solid move.

384
00:19:30,630 --> 00:19:33,850
You know, this right here is a chart of a nice move down.

